+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index | On-site HTTPS directory, managed search service | Predictable lookups with no network dependency. Each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index when snapshots arrive, keeping all registry logic self-contained. Avoids service timeout handling and recurring costs. |
+| Import atomicity mechanism | File-level replacement of SQLite database | In-place SQL transaction with rollback, dual-database swap with flag file | Atomic file rename ensures lookup never sees partial state. Simpler than dual-database coordination and more reliable than transaction rollback across process restarts. |
+| Index rebuild timing | Synchronous during import | Background rebuild with version flag | Import completes before the UI returns control. Technicians see clear success/failure immediately rather than wondering if a background job finished. 90,000 records rebuild in seconds; async complexity is not warranted. |
+
